                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes the signature of RerouteActions.execute() from\n`static final CompletableFuture<Long> execute(...)` (package-private) to\n`public static CompletableFuture<Long> execute(...)`, fixing a compile error\ncaused by the method being inaccessible from outside its declaring package.\n\ncandidate_02 is the commit that introduced this bug. It creates the new file\nsql/src/main/java/io/crate/executor/transport/RerouteActions.java, which\ndefines `execute()` without an access modifier (package-private), placing it\nin package io.crate.executor.transport. In the same commit, it also modifies\nsql/src/main/java/io/crate/action/sql/DDLStatementDispatcher.java (package\nio.crate.action.sql \u2014 a different package) to call\n`RerouteActions.execute(rerouteAction::execute, analysis, parameters)` in the\nvisitRerouteMoveShard and visitRerouteAllocateReplicaShard methods.\n\nBecause `execute()` is package-private and DDLStatementDispatcher lives in a\ndifferent package, this call would not compile \u2014 exactly the compile error\nthat the fix commit resolves by adding the `public` modifier.\n\ncandidate_01 only touches CHANGES.txt (documentation) and is unrelated to the\ncompile error.\n"
